// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_scene_own_placement.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: `scene()`'s POSITION guard on the per-layer deform ref
// (engine/level/scene_dsl.emp, P3 Task 9): `SceneDeform.Own(..)` is a per-LAYER
// attachment and a SCENE-level slot must refuse it.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "deform: Own(..) is a PER-LAYER attachment"
//
// WHY THIS GUARD EXISTS AT ALL, i.e. what goes wrong without it. `SceneDeform` is one
// enum authored in two positions, and the two accept different variants. A scene-level
// slot lowers to `pcfg_deform_table_fg` / `pcfg_deform_table_bg` — ONE table word per
// plane for the whole config, with no band to carry a per-layer speed. Without this
// ensure, `scene(deform_bg: Own(tbl, 15, 2, 0, 4))` would lower SILENTLY and
// SUCCESSFULLY: `scene_deform_table()` returns the Label from the Own arm just as it does
// from the Shared arm, so the table would land in the header and the shifts, the phase
// and the SPEED would be dropped on the floor with no diagnostic. That is the exact
// failure mode a `Label = 0` sentinel produces elsewhere in this tree, arrived at by a
// different route, and it is why the discrimination is on the VARIANT.
//
// THE TWO-FIXTURE DIFFERENTIAL. A guard that always fires is indistinguishable from one
// that works, so the module proves the position rule both ways:
//
//   FIXTURE A — the SAME table and speed authored the LEGAL way, `Shared(0, 4)`, in the
//               same scene-level slot. It must build and fold to $0000 (a table is
//               attached, which raises nothing since CAP_PER_LINE was retired; no live
//               amplitude anywhere, so no CAP_DEFORM). Two
//               ensures assert that and MUST STAY GREEN.
//   FIXTURE B — the same scene with the same payload spelled `Own(0, 15, 2, 0, 4)` in
//               that scene-level slot. One diagnostic, from scene()'s position guard.
//
// EXPECTED COUNT 1. Fixture B trips scene()'s position ensure and NOTHING ELSE, and that
// is worth stating because it is not obvious: with the Own in a scene slot there is no
// per-LAYER own anywhere, so `derived_own()` is 0, the scene-level-table guard does not
// fire, and `scene_caps()` classifies B exactly as it classifies A (a table is attached —
// `scene_deform_is_none()` is 0 for both Shared and Own). A count of 2 means a second
// guard started firing and this case is no longer isolating the position rule; a count of
// 0 means a scene-level slot now accepts a per-layer attachment.
//
// The null Label payload is poison_scene_mask.emp's convention and for its reason: every
// rule under test discriminates on the variant, never on the payload.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_scene_own_placement

use engine.level.scene_dsl.*
use engine.level.parallax_dsl.*

// FIXTURE A — the legal spelling of a scene-wide table.
const POISON_OWNPLACE_SCENE_A: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 3,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(0, 4))

// FIXTURE B — the same payload in the same slot, spelled as the per-layer variant.
const POISON_OWNPLACE_SCENE_B: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 3,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Own(0, 15, 2, 0, 4))

// Fixture A's capabilities, derived by hand: a table is attached (no bit — CAP_PER_LINE
// retired 2026-08-26); every amplitude shift is 15, so no CAP_DEFORM; no column table, no
// anchor, no per-layer table.
const POISON_OWNPLACE_DECLARED = $0000
const POISON_OWNPLACE_FOLDED_A = fold_caps([POISON_OWNPLACE_SCENE_A])
const POISON_OWNPLACE_FOLDED_B = fold_caps([POISON_OWNPLACE_SCENE_B])

// ---- FIXTURE A, THE PASSING HALF ----
ensure(POISON_OWNPLACE_FOLDED_A == POISON_OWNPLACE_DECLARED,
       "poison_scene_own_placement: FIXTURE A folds to {POISON_OWNPLACE_FOLDED_A}, not the hand-derived {POISON_OWNPLACE_DECLARED} — the LEGAL spelling of a scene-wide table stopped building the scene this poison contrasts against, so the refusal below proves nothing about position")

// ---- FIXTURE B, THE POISON ----
// The reference is what elaborates scene() for fixture B; the diagnostic comes from
// INSIDE scene(), not from this ensure, which is why the ensure's own text is a
// tautology-with-a-purpose rather than the message the lane matches.
ensure(POISON_OWNPLACE_FOLDED_B >= 0,
       "poison_scene_own_placement: unreachable — this ensure exists only to reference fixture B and force scene() to elaborate it")
